From: armSeb <armSeb@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: mmcc-msm8974: don't park mdp_clk_src at registration

mdp_clk_src uses clk_rcg2_shared_ops, whose .init parks the RCG on XO
when the clock is registered. When the bootloader leaves the display
running (continuous splash, used by simple-framebuffer/simpledrm), this
drops the MDP core clock from 240 MHz (GPLL0/2.5, CFG=0x504) to
19.2 MHz under the live scanout: the MDP underflows within the first
second of boot and the panel shows a solid color.

A regmap trace of the mmcc probe on the LG G3 (D855) shows this as the
only write that affects the display: CFG 0x2044 0x504 -> 0x0. MMPLL1 and
MMPLL3, which are reprogrammed too, were off.

Use clk_rcg2_shared_no_init_park_ops: the clock keeps its bootloader
configuration until a consumer (the MDSS driver) takes it over, and
parking on disable is kept.

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8974.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8974.c
index a0f7a9116..5c3a5ad26 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8974.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8974.c
@@ -486,7 +486,7 @@ static struct clk_rcg2 mdp_clk_src = {
 		.name = "mdp_clk_src",
 		.parent_data = mmcc_xo_mmpll0_dsi_hdmi_gpll0,
 		.num_parents = ARRAY_SIZE(mmcc_xo_mmpll0_dsi_hdmi_gpll0),
-		.ops = &clk_rcg2_shared_ops,
+		.ops = &clk_rcg2_shared_no_init_park_ops,
 	},
 };
 
